/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.

    Written to attack the store rules (2026-11-17 review): store into argument of recursion. A rabbit's series reaches
    something that outlives the rabbit (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to bury-in, given (the series of series of number bag, the number deep):
    If deep is 0:
        Insert (a series of number with (1, 2, 3)) into bag.
        Return.
    Done.
    Cast bury-in on (bag, deep - 1).
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast bury-in on (keeper, 3).
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper.
